findings.user_instructions:
Take the finding's second, non-rewriting path. History rewriting is not supported by this pipeline: its guard aborts the whole run when the worktree HEAD stops being a descendant of the run's recorded head, so an amend, rebase, squash, reset, or force here fails the run instead of fixing the finding. Do not attempt one. Every commit you create must be a normal descendant of the current HEAD, with the existing commits left exactly as they are.

Add one commit whose message carries a full body stating, plainly and in full sentences:

- this change pins the fixture reap bound and its fail-first regression only;
- bin/fm-watch.sh is byte-identical to the base branch, so no watcher stop-path change ships here;
- test_stop_terminates_a_poll_in_flight pins existing stop-path behavior rather than validating a fix;
- a TERM lost shortly after a background fork (measured 2 of 150 runs on the authoring host) is not reproduced or fixed here, and is filed as follow-up lesson-f16b;
- this message explicitly supersedes the earlier commit 708c332 paragraph that claimed bin/fm-watch.sh installs one stop handler once and never swaps it, which is no longer true.

If the fix round finds no file change to make - bin/fm-watch.sh is already reverted to base and no test needs editing - then carry those statements as the body of the commit itself; an otherwise content-empty commit is acceptable here, because the finding asks for the statement on the branch rather than for a code change. Do not invent code, comment, or test changes to fill it, and do not touch bin/fm-watch.sh or any test assertion.

Also make sure the same five statements appear plainly in the pull request description this run produces.

findings.description:
`OPTION` only ends an option at `;` before the next `(x)`, at `. Recommendation`, or at the end of the string. When options are written as bullet lines (`Options:
- (a) Play
- (b) App Store
Recommendation: (b).`), the parser returns one option, key `a`, with text `"Play
- (b) App Store"`. The recommendation is still `b`, so the recommended option has no button and the card offers one merged, wrong choice. Fix: also end an option at a newline or bullet before the next `(x)`, for example lookahead `(?=[;
]\s*(?:[-*]\s*)?\([a-z]\)|…)`, and strip bullet markers.

